From: Vinayak Katoch <vkatoch@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Jan 2026 15:47:02 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Add SELinux policy for CDSP RPC daemon

Define security policy for cdsprpcd daemon (/usr/bin/cdsprpcd) that
manages FastRPC communication with the CDSP subsystem.

Create new policy module qcom_cdsprpcd with daemon domain and required
permissions for CDSP device access, DMA operations, and system integration.

- qcom_cdsprpcd.fc: Label cdsprpcd executable as qcom_cdsprpcd_exec_t
- qcom_cdsprpcd.te: Define qcom_cdsprpcd_t daemon domain with permissions:
  * Unix datagram socket creation and sendto for logging
  * CDSP device access (secure /dev/fastrpc-cdsp-secure and non-secure
    /dev/fastrpc-cdsp) via qcom_cdsp_*_read_device() interfaces
  * DMA heap device access (/dev/dma_heap/system) for shared memory
  * Sysfs reading for device tree model information
  * Configuration file reading from /usr/share/qcom/
  * Directory watching (inotify) for /dev, /usr/lib, and /usr/share
  * Runtime directory search and syslog messaging
  * Localization file access
- qcom_cdsprpcd.if: Placeholder interface file for future extensions

The policy uses interface macros from devices.if for clean abstraction
and maintainability. All device access permissions (getattr, ioctl) are
provided automatically through read_chr_files_pattern() and
rw_chr_files_pattern() macros.

Signed-off-by: Vinayak Katoch <vkatoch@qti.qualcomm.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Qualcomm specific change]
